				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1604,
				42
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add VS Code service interfaces for Commands, Editor, Extensions, Files, Language, and TextFile\n\nIntroduce six new service abstractions to Wind's Effect-TS based service layer, each modeled after corresponding VS Code services:\n\n- **CommandsService**: ICommandService for command registration/execution\n- **EditorService**: ICodeEditorService for editor lifecycle and selection management\n- **ExtensionsService**: IExtensionService for extension discovery and activation\n- **FilesService**: IFileService for file system operations\n- **LanguageService**: ILanguageService for language feature providers\n- **TextFileService**: ITextFileService for text file read/write/save operations\n\nEach service includes:\n- Interface definition with Effect-returning methods\n- Problem type for error modeling via discriminated unions\n- Context tag for Effect-TS dependency injection\n- Stub implementation for compile-time compatibility\n- Live and Mock Layer configurations\n\nThese interfaces establish the foundational service boundaries for Wind's re-implementation of VS Code's workbench services.",
			"SHA": "25265a307b53113e827858cacf603cc2c680b709"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T07:18:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1532,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Rewrite README for conciseness and clarity\n\nReplace the verbose README with a problem/solution narrative. The introduction now leads with the Electron IPC pain point and the \"no IPC proxy\" value proposition. Consolidates \"Key Features\" and \"Core Architecture Principles\" into a brief \"What It Does\" section. Removes the detailed getting started guide, code examples, and changelog — content better suited for external documentation at editor.land. Updates vendor badge images to use locally hosted editor.land SVGs (Tauri.svg, EffectTS.svg) instead of external simpleicons.org URLs. Refreshes \"See Also\" links to point to the new documentation structure.\n\nThe README now serves as a quick reference rather than a comprehensive guide.",
			"SHA": "4d16188db2de9edb1b98f513393b56052d8c8e0b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T07:08:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1532,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Wind): Add vendor icons to Tauri and Effect-TS badges in README\n\nPrepend inline SVG vendor icons from simpleicons.org to the existing shields.io badges for Tauri and Effect-TS dependencies. This enhances visual branding and makes the dependency list more immediately recognizable at a glance.",
			"SHA": "f58c451947f4306b6adfac11b7c9e4368cd43ea0"
		},
